{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And he removed —</b> the Egyptian — <b>the wheel of his chariot.</b> Like the expression 'and he turned aside to her, the tent' (Judges 4:18). The Egyptian seeks to turn the chariot backward to flee, as he explains: <b>and drove him laboriously</b> — the thing was too heavy for him to turn backward, for the chariot of his fellow going behind him blocks the chariot of his that goes first from turning back, and in this order all of them block one another; and when the Egyptians saw this, <b>and the Egyptian said: Let me flee</b> on foot and abandon the chariot, <b>from before Israel</b> — and even this did not avail them, as it is written: 'And HaShem said to Moses: Stretch out your hand over the sea,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:53.477403818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}